{
  "context": "For each work unit:\n1. Read each file in the cluster to identify all raw print() call sites.\n2. For each site, replace print(\"...\") with emit(\"...\") - the signatures are\n   identical for simple string output.\n3. For f-string or multi-arg print() calls, preserve formatting: emit() accepts\n   any Rich renderable or plain string, so f-strings pass through unchanged.\n4. Add `from benchbox.utils.printing import emit` to the imports if not present.\n   Remove any now-unused imports (e.g., `from rich.console import Console` if\n   the Console instance was only used for print-equivalent calls).\n5. After completing the cluster, remove those file paths from _PENDING_MIGRATION\n   in tests/unit/cli/test_output_control_static.py.\n6. Run the static guardrail test to confirm: `uv run -- python -m pytest\n   tests/unit/cli/test_output_control_static.py -v`.\n7. Commit the cluster migration + _PENDING_MIGRATION removal atomically.\n\nImportant notes:\n- Some files may use print() for debug/development output that should simply\n  be removed rather than migrated (e.g., worker_pool_examples.py which is\n  example/demo code). Evaluate each site: if it's debug output with no\n  user-facing value, delete it; if it's user-facing status, migrate to emit().\n- Tuning generators (w8) likely use print() for DDL output that users pipe to\n  files.  These may need emit() with appropriate formatting, or may need a\n  separate stdout-clean path.  Read each generator before deciding.\n- TPC-DI worker_pool_examples.py is almost certainly example/demo code; its\n  print() calls may be intentional and should be evaluated for removal vs migration.\n",
  "description": "The centralize-output-control effort (completed 2026-02-18) migrated the high-traffic\nCLI/core/TPC-DS/MCP paths to emit() and added a global ratchet test that prevents new\nprint() leaks.  However, the ratchet discovered 68 pre-existing files that were out of\nscope for that effort and placed in _PENDING_MIGRATION.\n\nThis TODO drives the migration of all 68 files, subsystem by subsystem, until\n_PENDING_MIGRATION is empty and the global guardrail covers the entire codebase.\n\nFiles are grouped into 12 work units by subsystem to keep each session focused:\n  w1  - utils layer         (5 files)\n  w2  - CLI help            (1 file)\n  w3  - analysis + comparison  (5 files)\n  w4  - cost + misc core    (8 files)\n  w5  - dataframe cluster   (5 files)\n  w6  - TPC-DI cluster      (7 files)\n  w7  - TPC-DS misc + TPC-H skew  (5 files)\n  w8  - tuning generators   (11 files)\n  w9  - publishing cluster  (4 files)\n  w10 - monitoring cluster  (5 files)\n  w11 - platforms cluster   (8 files)\n  w12 - release + primitives                (4 files)\n  w13 - remove all entries from _PENDING_MIGRATION, verify clean\n\nAfter w13 the ratchet test enforces zero tolerance automatically - no future\nmaintenance required.",
  "legacy": {
